{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>And came Moses and spoke,</b> etc. This is what was stated above: 'And Moses spoke in the ears of all the congregation of Israel,' etc." "<b>He and Hoshea son of Nun.</b> For HaShem commanded both of them, as it is written 'Take for yourself Joshua,' and it is written 'And now, write for yourselves this song and teach it to the children of Israel.' <b>And Hoshea son of Nun:</b> at first, when he entered to be the attendant of Moses, Moses called him Joshua, for such is the way of kings to change the name of their attendants — for example, Joseph, Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah. And now, when he became king, he reverted to his original name. Even so, in all of Scripture he is called Joshua, because he was already accustomed to it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:17.607135494Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}